meta {
  name: 14_FilterMatchAll
  seq: 14
}

docs {
  Scenario: match=all only returns clients holding every filter package

    Given the CCR client and the rightholder client both grant the facilitator the
      skattegrunnlag package on a rightholder relation
    When the client list is filtered by the regnskapsforer-lonn and skattegrunnlag
      packages
    Then both clients are returned in the default any mode
    And match=all returns only the CCR client, which holds the lonn package
      through its role and the skattegrunnlag package through the delegation

  The CCR client is the one case that needs both ways in at once: the lonn package
  comes from the regnskapsforer role, the skattegrunnlag package from the grant the
  scenario sets up. The rightholder client drops out of the all mode unless it is a
  CCR client of the facilitator too, which the test data records per environment
  (client_B.alsoCcrClientOfFacilitator). What proves the filter is the facilitator's
  other CCR clients: they hold only the lonn package, appear in the any mode and must
  not appear with match=all. The scenario removes both rightholder relations it created.
}
